# Offline Workout Tracking: Local Storage and Conflict Resolution

![Offline workout tracking with local storage, queued synchronization, and conflict resolution](./offline-workout-tracking.png)

## Overview

Offline workout tracking lets users record exercises, sets, repetitions, and session completion without waiting for a network connection.

This matters in basement gyms, outdoor training locations, and any environment where connectivity is unreliable. A remote-only save can fail, time out, or finish after the app has closed.

An offline-first mobile app saves changes locally, updates the interface from durable local data, and synchronizes separately.

The central reliability requirement is straightforward: a failed request must not erase a workout, and a successful retry must not create a duplicate.

This guide assumes a SQLite-backed mobile database. TypeScript-style pseudocode illustrates application logic rather than an existing package API. The snippets have not been compiled or tested.

